  "summary": "DIR-087 Phase 1 complete - the escalation is fixed, the guard that let it slip is widened, and the inventory/benchmark/scorecard deliverables are produced from a reproducible collector. S1 THE ESCALATION: a repo-wide sweep found EXACTLY ONE remaining no-op scrollbar class at src/components/JobsListings/JobSearchBar.jsx:188 (the Quick Trending Filter Pills strip) - a no-op because package.json pins tailwindcss ^4.1.8 with NO scrollbar plugin, so it emitted no CSS. Fixed with the plugin-free arbitrary form [scrollbar-width:none] plus [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden; the strip stays scrollable and keyboard reachable. This is the fourth and last occurrence - DIR-086 fixed the other three. S2 THE GUARD: DIR-086 AC3 hard-coded three file paths, which is exactly why this fourth occurrence survived its own directive. AC2 now walks every .jsx/.js/.css under src (707 files) and asserts the class appears in no className and no stylesheet. Deliberate design choice: the guard targets className values and CSS rather than raw text, so the documentation comments that explain the removal may legitimately name the class - a blunt whole-file text scan would punish the very comments that prevent recurrence. S3 INVENTORY: 14 candidate surfaces inventoried with measured line counts emitted by the collector (Overview 1942, Resume Builder shell 2710, Cover Letters 1812, Portfolios 548, Job Tracker 1075, Applied Jobs 553, Job Portal 873, Job Search Bar 224, AI Interview Coach 3130, Messages 675, Settings & 2FA 6171, Support 863, Executive Rail 91, Portfolio Gallery 239). THE MOST IMPORTANT FINDING IS AN ERROR OF MY OWN THAT THE TESTS CAUGHT: the router is SPLIT ACROSS THREE FILES - src/main.jsx owns public routes, DashboardMain.jsx owns every /dashboard child, and BuildResume.jsx owns the /build-resume steps - so my first inventory draft read only main.jsx, found no job-portal route, and wrongly reported that /jobs/portal and /jobs/browse were unmounted. The new AC3 failed and exposed it. The truth is those routes DO exist at src/main.jsx:594-598 as ABSOLUTE paths and they are AUTH-AWARE DISPATCHERS: a guest gets MainJobListings rendered in place, while a signed-in candidate is redirected into /dashboard/jobs. Both path families are real and a crawler must follow the redirect. I corrected the inventory rather than quietly dropping the claim. Two further brief corrections held: there is no DashboardPlans module (/dashboard/plans is served by Billing) and /dashboard/favorites is served by DashboardFavourites. /dashboard/profile and /dashboard/security are REDIRECTS into settings tabs, not pages. The brief says the builder has 10 steps; the router mounts THIRTEEN children (11 step components plus an index alias plus a review screen), so auditing only the ten named steps would have missed custom and review. FROZEN BASELINE: the 55 figure is 55 TEMPLATE MODULES (cv1..cv51 plus cover1..cover4); a raw file count returns 67 because each template directory holds nested files, and AC4 pins the module count. S4 BENCHMARKS: Linear, Teal HQ, Rezi and Kickresume were researched from their own published material and cited. HIRED IS NO LONGER A LIVE PRODUCT - hired.com/how-it-works now redirects to LHH (the Adecco Group), which lists Hired nowhere in its product set - so I recorded that rather than inventing a feature set. Where a dimension could not be verified the cell says Not verified on purpose, including every vendor performance budget. The most transferable lesson is Rezi's: ATS-safe formatting is applied as you type, not after, which is the opposite of IME365 surfacing an ATS score on a separate surface. S5 SCORING: derived, never hand-assigned, from score = 10 * (0.50*tokenAdoption + 0.25*responsive + 0.25*guards), where tokenAdoption = cubaClasses / (cubaClasses + legacyColourUtilities), responsive = distinctBreakpoints / 5, and guards = (loadingUi + emptyUi + errorUi) / 3. COMPOSITE 5.7/10. Worst surfaces: Job Search Bar 2.5, Settings & 2FA 3.7, Support 4.0, Resume Builder 4.3, Job Portal 4.5, AI Interview Coach 4.5. Best: Job Tracker 8.7, Portfolio Gallery 9.0. The shape matches DIR-081 - newer purpose-built surfaces are genuinely tokenised while the oldest and largest bodies remain legacy. TWO P0 BLOCKERS: Settings & 2FA carries 1340 legacy colour utilities in a 6171-line body and AI Interview Coach carries 803 in a 3130-line body, plus 17 P1 findings. I ALSO FOUND AND FIXED A DEFECT IN MY OWN DETECTOR: the first guard detector matched only the component names CubaSkeleton/CubaEmptyState/CubaErrorState and therefore reported DashboardMessages as having NO guards, even though it renders bespoke loading and error states from isLoadingMessages/messagesError. That was a false P0; the detector now matches what actually paints and the false finding was removed rather than reported. HONEST CAVEATS CARRIED IN THE SCORECARD: the breakpoint proxy can under-rate a page that delegates responsiveness to its shell; and these legacy counts are a SUPERSET of the DIR-082 counter because they also match shadow/fill/stroke/decoration/accent/caret prefixes and the zinc/neutral/stone/violet/fuchsia families - which is why Settings reads 1340 here versus 1330 there and Interview Coach 803 versus 764. These are NOT regressions, they are the same code measured by a wider lens. S6 DELIVERABLES: .bridge/evidence/dir087-candidate-page-inventory.md, .bridge/evidence/dir087-baseline-quality-scorecard.md, .bridge/evidence/dir087-metrics.mjs (the reproducible collector) and tests/dir087-candidate-master-audit.test.mjs with 6 acceptance tests, registered as test:dir087. VERIFIED: dir087 6 passing; 136 passing across dir087 + dir086 + dir085 + dir084 + dir083 + dir082 + dir081 + dir079 + dir077 + dir048 suites + dir055 + cuba-candidate-portal + cuba-design-system + unlayered-css-guard; test:dir072..dir087 and test:design-system every script EXIT 0; test:product EXIT 0 on a quiet run; security:static 67 passing; xampp-policy 4 passing; build EXIT 0 in 2.78s measured with no concurrent load against a 4.0s budget; lint 0 errors with 256 warnings unchanged project-wide; frozen src/cv-templates diff 0 against the DIR-086 certified commit 56f4df06. MEASUREMENT NOTE: an earlier build reading of 4.45s was taken immediately after the full product suite finished on the same machine; quiet, the build is 2.78s. SCOPE HELD: Phase 1 is inventory, benchmarks, baseline scoring, the escalated fix and the guard - I did NOT refactor any page body, so the 2 P0 and 17 P1 findings are for remediation phases that should each be their own directive so every change is independently verifiable."
